    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Ryan are delighted to present Lochinvar, Broghill Road, Charleville, Co. Cork to the market for sale.\n\nThis detached three-bedroom bungalow occupies a generous c. 0.3-acre site in one of Charleville's most convenient and sought-after residential locations. Set on the outskirts of the town, the property enjoys a wonderfully peaceful and serene setting, while remaining within easy walking distance of shops, schools, sporting facilities and public transport.\n\nLochinvar offers a fantastic renovation opportunity for purchasers looking to create a home that is truly their own. The property is in need of modernisation and upgrading throughout, but the generous accommodation, substantial site and excellent location provide an outstanding foundation for what could become a beautiful dream home in a tranquil setting.\n\nThe accommodation is spacious and well proportioned, with excellent potential to reconfigure and modernise to suit individual requirements. Outside, the property benefits from a large driveway with ample parking, a garage, useful outbuildings and generous gardens to both the front and rear.\n\nThe mature rear garden provides a private and peaceful space with plenty of scope for landscaping, entertaining, gardening or family enjoyment. The overall site offers excellent potential for creating an attractive outdoor setting to complement the renovated home.\n\nThe location is a particular feature of Lochinvar. Broghill Road is a well-established residential area on the edge of Charleville, offering the best of both worlds — a quiet, scenic and private environment with the convenience of the town and its amenities close at hand. The property also provides easy access to the road network connecting Charleville with Cork, Limerick and surrounding towns.\n\nWhile the property requires renovation, it is easy to see the potential to transform Lochinvar into a superb family home in a wonderfully serene setting. For those willing to undertake the necessary works, this is an opportunity to create a home tailored to their own style and requirements.\n\nVacant and chain free, Lochinvar is ready for its next chapter. Early viewing is highly recommended to appreciate the setting, site and enormous potential this property has to offer.\n\nAccommodation\nKitchen/Dining Room: 2.9m x 7.5m\nLiving Room: 4.4m x 3.6m\nBedroom 1: 3.4m x 3.6m\nBedroom 2: 3.6m x 3.1m\nBedroom 3: 3.6m x 3.1m\nBathroom: 2.3m x 1.9m\n\nKey Features\nDetached three-bedroom bungalow\nC. 0.3-acre site\nExcellent renovation opportunity\nIn need of modernisation and upgrading\nPotential to create a dream home\nPeaceful and serene residential setting\nGenerous front and rear gardens\nMature and private site\nLarge driveway with ample off-street parking\nGarage and useful outbuildings\nWalking distance to Charleville town\nClose to shops, schools, sporting facilities and public transport\nVacant and chain free\nOil-fired central heating\nExcellent access to Cork, Limerick and surrounding areas\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the potential, generous site and peaceful setting of this property.\n\nThese particulars have been prepared by DNG John Ryan and whilst every care has been taken to ensure that these are accurate and correct, we are not responsible for any errors, omissions, inaccuracies, if the property is let, sold or withdrawn from sale or if it is not suitable for your purpose. These particulars are for information only and are given under the strict understanding that they do not form part of any contract. Neither whole nor any part of this document or any reference thereto may be included in any public document, circular or statement nor published without the written consent of DNG John Ryan. PSL: 003615"
      },
